n affect the gravity field. Navigation used radio range and Doppler measurements alongside spacecraft observations."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"A uniform spherical teaching model cannot reproduce Eros operations. Measurements and planned corrections matter."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","A uniform spherical teaching model cannot reproduce Eros operations. Measurements and planned corrections matter."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Stay nearby, then look closer"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"NEAR entered orbit on February 14, 2000. The team changed orbits for different observations: by April 30 the operational distance was about 50 km from the centre; a July phase used about 35 km from the centre."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"Centre distance is not surface clearance. An irregular surface changes the gap underneath an orbit. The displayed loops are schematic, not measured trajectories."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","Centre distance is not surface clearance. An irregular surface changes the gap underneath an orbit. The displayed loops are schematic, not measured trajectories."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Pictures and reflected light"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"The Multi-Spectral Imager mapped morphology and colour differences. The Near Infrared Spectrometer measured reflected infrared light to investigate minerals. A May 2000 power problem ended NIS operations."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"A photograph can reveal structure; spectral measurements help interpret materials. No single view supplies every answer."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","A photograph can reveal structure; spectral measurements help interpret materials. No single view supplies every answer."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Six ways to ask about a rock"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"X-ray/gamma-ray spectroscopy probes elemental composition. The laser rangefinder measures distance for shape and topography. The magnetometer investigates magnetic fields. Radio tracking constrains motion, gravity and mass distribution."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"Combine complementary measurements rather than assigning every result to a camera. Radio science uses communications tracking, not a separate camera."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","Combine complementary measurements rather than assigning every result to a camera. Radio science uses communications tracking, not a separate camera."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://pds.nasa.gov/ds-view/pds/viewProfile.jsp?dsid=NEAR-A-RSS-1%2F5-EROS%2FORBIT-V1.0","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA PDS radio science archive"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"An orbiter, deliberately brought down"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"The spacecraft had no purpose-built landing gear. After a year of orbital study, planners chose a slow controlled descent on February 12, 2001. It photographed the surface on the way down and survived contact."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"Not designed as a lander does not mean an accidental crash. A planned descent managed risk without guaranteeing survival."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","Not designed as a lander does not mean an accidental crash. A planned descent managed risk without guaranteeing survival."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jhuapl.edu/destinations/missions/near","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"JHUAPL spacecraft and teams"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"South of Himeros"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"NASA describes touchdown south of the saddle-shaped Himeros region. The official landing-site mosaic shows the planned site with south toward the top."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"This STL has no verified registration to the published geographic frame. Use the official image for regional context; there is no exact geographic pin on our mesh."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","This STL has no verified registration to the published geographic frame. Use the official image for regional context; there is no exact geographic pin on our mesh."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/location-of-the-near-shoemaker-landing-site/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL/JHUAPL landing-site image"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/near-shoemaker/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA mission history"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"The signal after contact"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"The orbiter survived touchdown. On February 14 NASA announced an extension for gamma-ray measurements and prioritised their recovery over other recorder data using the reliable low-gain link."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Why this matters"],["P",{},"Close surface proximity offered a valuable opportunity to investigate surface and subsurface composition. A working link and careful data priorities made survival scientifically useful."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","Close surface proximity offered a valuable opportunity to investigate surface and subsurface composition. A working link and careful data priorities made survival scientifically useful."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/near-shoemaker-ready-to-gather-data-on-surface-of-eros/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA surface science announcement"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"The last transmission was not the last result"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"NEAR Shoemaker / 433 Eros"],["P",{},"Last contact was February 28, 2001. NEAR established asteroid orbiting and landing milestones and left a recor